## Conversation
Extend the default effort option in PR 668 to DeepSeek V4, GPT-OSS, GLM-5.2 and GLM-5.3, Beam, and Muse Glimmer. Preserve each model's normal generation prompt and explicit effort.

## Actions
Inspected each model's stock effort instruction and supplied argument. Extended the native V4 formatter and adapted the relevant executable Jinja blocks at template load. Added request-path tests and documented the supported templates with pinned upstream sources. On Rust 1.96.1, 370 renderer tests passed with 2 ignored, and formatting and Clippy passed. An independent program compared the complete stock GPT-OSS 20B/120B, GLM-5.2/5.3/5.3-Flash, Beam, and Muse Glimmer templates with the public renderer, with and without tools and a system message. Default and explicit prompts were byte-identical to the baseline. Opt-out removed only the native default directive.

## Errors & Mistakes
The initial DeepSeek regression failed because the original renderer still inserted the high prefix. A draft Jinja context expression failed with "no rules expected `..`". The explicit-effort test then exposed an incorrect map precedence assumption. MiniJinja merge_maps gives the last matching map precedence.

